From: MridaOS Dev <darpan@mridaos.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:29:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?design:=20complete=20UI=20overhaul=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20new=20design=20system=20+=20animations?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Design system (index.css):
- Replace all hardcoded hex values with CSS custom properties (--m-* tokens)
- New palette: Ink, Stone, Forest, Brass — earthy agri identity, not generic SaaS green
- Proper dark mode: tokens redefine at .dark, no more !important override wars
- Animation system: m-fade-up, m-slide-up, m-pop-in, m-stagger, m-shimmer
- Correct easing: cubic-bezier(0.23,1,0.32,1) for all UI, never ease-in
- Skeleton loader utility class
- Semantic component classes: m-card, m-btn, m-input, m-badge, m-nav-item
- prefers-reduced-motion respected on all animations
- hover: pointer:fine gating on all hover transforms

Sidebar:
- Remove emerald-950 hardcoded dark background
- Grouped nav with section labels (Operations / Intelligence / Compliance / Other)
- Token-based active state (no more hardcoded emerald shades)
- ARIA: role=navigation, aria-label, aria-current=page on active item
- Clean brand mark: leaf icon + wordmark, no gradient panels

TopBar:
- Token-based colors throughout, dark mode works without !important
- Cleaner layout: 12px height reduction, better information density
- ARIA labels on all icon buttons
- Consistent button sizing with m-btn system

LoginPage:
- Remove gradient hero panel — replaced with flat forest-green brand panel
- Remove decorative blur circles and AI-aesthetic choices
- Proper form accessibility: htmlFor/id pairs, aria-live error region, aria-label on icon buttons
- Entry animation (m-fade-up) on the card
- No hardcoded hex anywhere

App.tsx:
- Remove Lenis smooth scroll (wrong tool for a billing terminal)
- Remove containerRef/contentRef wiring
- Loading screen uses CSS tokens

Fixes:
- TS error: stock_qty → stockQty in CropVisionSecurityView
- TS error: addOperationalAlert → setAlerts with typed OperationalAlert
